1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,574
Spring Boot assembles a Spring application using starters, auto-configuration, and external configuration.

2
00:00:06,724 --> 00:00:11,867
Auto-configuration reacts to classes, properties, and existing beans; it is not magic

3
00:00:11,867 --> 00:00:15,296
and can be inspected when behavior is unexpected.

4
00:00:15,446 --> 00:00:20,142
Use the dependency management supplied by the chosen Boot release instead of

5
00:00:20,142 --> 00:00:21,708
independently mixing framework versions.

6
00:00:21,858 --> 00:00:25,154
Keep environment-specific values outside source code.

7
00:00:25,304 --> 00:00:31,668
Profiles can select local and PostgreSQL settings, while environment variables supply connection

8
00:00:31,668 --> 00:00:32,198
details.

9
00:00:32,348 --> 00:00:35,093
Validate required configuration at startup.

10
00:00:35,243 --> 00:00:40,130
Secrets should come from an appropriate secret store or injected environment, never

11
00:00:40,130 --> 00:00:41,759
a committed repository file.

12
00:00:41,909 --> 00:00:45,873
Both services pin Boot 4.0.9 and Java 21.

13
00:00:46,023 --> 00:00:51,061
The default profile binds only to 127.0.0.1 and uses an in-memory H2

14
00:00:51,061 --> 00:00:51,480
database.

15
00:00:51,630 --> 00:00:56,705
The postgres profile reads DB_URL, DB_USER, and DB_PASSWORD.

16
00:00:56,855 --> 00:01:01,350
Flyway creates the schema, while Hibernate validates that the mappings match it.

17
00:01:01,500 --> 00:01:04,270
Restarting the default profile resets its data.

18
00:01:04,420 --> 00:01:07,725
Run a service with a different port supplied on the command line.

19
00:01:07,875 --> 00:01:12,541
Then intentionally provide an invalid database URL and inspect the startup failure.

20
00:01:12,691 --> 00:01:16,345
Explain which settings should vary between development and production.

21
00:01:16,495 --> 00:01:23,669
Ports, database endpoints, credentials, timeouts, and observability destinations vary by environment.

22
00:01:23,819 --> 00:01:27,434
Business invariants should not silently change through profiles.

23
00:01:27,584 --> 00:01:32,849
Keep a documented configuration contract and avoid copying production credentials into a

24
00:01:32,849 --> 00:01:34,165
local properties file.

25
00:01:34,315 --> 00:01:34,987
Question.

26
00:01:35,137 --> 00:01:36,672
What does a starter provide?

27
00:01:36,822 --> 00:01:37,398
Answer.

28
00:01:37,548 --> 00:01:42,536
A coordinated dependency set and configuration integration for a capability such as

29
00:01:42,536 --> 00:01:44,198
web MVC or JPA.

30
00:01:44,348 --> 00:01:45,019
Question.

31
00:01:45,169 --> 00:01:47,412
Why pin a compatible version family?

32
00:01:47,562 --> 00:01:48,139
Answer.

33
00:01:48,289 --> 00:01:54,637
It reduces untested combinations of Spring, Hibernate, Jackson, and other managed dependencies.
